    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d929">

                <pb facs="1000" n="990" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg990"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">693.9431/6–349: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Consul General at Peiping</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Clubb</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-06-21T16:00:00-04:00">June 21, 1949—4 p.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>381. Question arrangements dispatch private trade delegation Japan referred SCAP
                    (ur 929 June 3<anchor n="83" xml:id="d929-f1"/>). Urinfo Dept doubts possibility
                    SCAP receive representatives local regime in any official capacity should they
                    desire proceed Japan,<anchor n="84" xml:id="d929-f2"/> and no encouragement shld
                    be given inquiry this regard.</p>
                <pb facs="1001" n="991" xml:id="pg991"/>
                <p>In this connection, suggest you indicate Chang Tsung-ping availability your
                    facilities for making prelim inquiry of SCAP concrete trade proposals; and that
                    such approach might avoid waste motion since it would provide SCAP better basis
                    on which to assess feasibility engage trade negots direct with trade
                    mission.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Webb</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d929-f1" n="83" xml:id="d929-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d929-f2" n="84" xml:id="d929-f2-content">
                <p>In telegram No. 235, July 6, the Counselor of Mission in Japan (Huston) reported
                    that “SCAP does not consider appropriate at this time entry into Japan either of
                    mission accompanied by representatives of Chinese Communist regime or of mission
                    without such representatives but comprised of Chinese nationals not officially
                    sponsored by Chinese Mission Tokyo” and that SCAP “has under consideration
                    several trial deals involving trade with North China which, it is expected, will
                    afford an indication as to pattern subsequent deals might take.”
                    (693.9431/7–649)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
